# Distributed Cops-and-Robbers over a Peer-to-Peer Network (Dec-POMDP)

[![Python 3.11+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.11+-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
[![FastMCP](https://img.shields.io/badge/MCP-FastMCP-green.svg)](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)

## Overview & Academic Summary
This project implements an autonomous, decentralized multi-agent system executing a **Distributed Cops-and-Robbers** game on a discrete $7 \times 7$ grid over a Peer-to-Peer (P2P) network using the **Model Context Protocol (MCP / FastMCP)**.

The system features two symmetric AI agent roles—**Police** (Cop) and **Robber** (Thief)—that interact autonomously without a central game server or neutral referee. Complete state integrity, turn synchronization, and zero-trust computational fairness are guaranteed via a 4-stage cryptographic **SHA-256 Commit-Reveal Protocol**.

---

## Dec-POMDP Mathematical Formalization
The game environment is formally defined as an 8-tuple Dec-POMDP:
$$\langle n, S, \{A_i\}, P, R, \{\Omega_i\}, O, \gamma \rangle$$

1. **Number of Agents ($n = 2$)**: Police Agent ($i=1$) and Thief Agent ($i=2$).
2. **State Space ($S$)**: Complete grid state $s = (pos_{cop}, pos_{thief}, B, T_{scent}, turn)$ where $B$ is the set of static barriers ($|B| \le 14$).
3. **Action Space ($A_i$)**: Orthogonal grid moves $A_i \in \{\text{N}, \text{S}, \text{E}, \text{W}, \text{STAY}\}$.
4. **Transition Function ($P$)**: Deterministic physical move updates subject to grid boundaries $[0..6] \times [0..6]$ and wall barriers.
5. **Reward Function ($R$)**:
   - Cop capture of Thief: Cop $+20$, Thief $-20$.
   - Thief survival up to turn 35: Thief $+10$, Cop $-5$.
   - Technical loss (protocol violation/cheat attempt): Violator $-20$.
6. **Observation Space ($\Omega_i$)**: Local observation tuple $\Omega_{cop} = (pos_{cop}, T_{scent\_local}, Hint_{verbal})$.
7. **Observation Function ($O$)**: Radial scent emission $\tau_{center} = 0.9$ with decay rate $\rho = 0.10$.
8. **Discount Factor ($\gamma = 0.95$)**: Discounted total cumulative return for finite horizon $T=35$.

