## Project Directory Layout
```
.
├── config/
│   ├── game.json             # Signed Shared Contract (7x7 grid, rules)
│   └── game.toml             # Private Per-Peer Settings (ports, LLM)
├── docs/
│   ├── features/             # Feature PRD, Plan, and Todo specifications
│   ├── instructions/         # Master PRD, PLAN, and TODO lists
│   ├── PRD_commit_reveal.md  # Mechanism PRD: Commit-Reveal
│   ├── PRD_bayesian_belief.md# Mechanism PRD: Bayesian Belief Grid
│   ├── PRD_scent_tracking.md # Mechanism PRD: Dynamic Scent Model
│   └── PRD_gatekeeper.md     # Mechanism PRD: Gatekeeper Rate Limiter
├── notebooks/
│   └── analysis.ipynb        # Jupyter Notebook sensitivity analysis
├── results/
│   └── benchmark_summary.json# Experiment benchmark outputs
├── assets/                   # Architecture diagrams & plots
├── src/
│   ├── automation/           # Gmail API reporting automation
│   ├── core/                 # Orchestrator & State Machine
│   ├── domain/               # Grid, Scent, Belief, Capture, Crypto
│   ├── gui/                  # Live Heatmap & Replay Verifier GUI
│   ├── infra/                # Rate Limiter & LLM Provider
│   ├── network/              # FastMCP Server wrapper
│   ├── p2p/                  # P2P Server implementation
│   ├── reliability/          # Watchdog & Deadline Tracker
│   └── strategy/             # PoliceBrain, ThiefBrain, Q-Learning
├── tests/                    # Comprehensive Pytest test suite
├── main.py                   # CLI Application Entry Point
├── pyproject.toml            # Root build & dependency configuration
└── uv.lock                   # Locked dependency manifest
```

---

## Installation & Setup Guide

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.11+
- `uv` (Fast Python package installer)

### Quick Start Commands
```bash
# 1. Install dependencies
uv sync

# 2. Run unit test suite
uv run pytest

# 3. Run Police Peer Server
python main.py peer --role police --port 8000

# 4. Run Thief Peer Server
python main.py peer --role thief --port 8001

# 5. Verify match log integrity
python main.py replay --log logs/police_match.json
```

